## HubSpot and PayPal backends

HubSpot and PayPal are running locally as mocks of the real APIs. They need no real credentials: any access token, client id and client secret is accepted.

- HubSpot base URL: `{{.HubSpotURL}}`
- PayPal base URL: `{{.PayPalURL}}`
- PayPal OAuth2 token endpoint (client credentials grant): `{{.PayPalURL}}/v1/oauth2/token`

If the target language is Ballerina, use the Ballerina connector packages `ballerinax/hubspot.crm.obj.contacts` (HubSpot), `ballerinax/paypal.orders` (PayPal) and `ballerinax/mysql` (MySQL). The connectors default to the real services' URLs, so set their `serviceUrl` to include the API prefix on the mock base URL: `{{.HubSpotURL}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts` for HubSpot (bearer token authentication) and `{{.PayPalURL}}/v2/checkout` for PayPal (OAuth2 client credentials with `tokenUrl` `{{.PayPalURL}}/v1/oauth2/token`). Use the connector clients' own request and response types. For other languages, call the REST endpoints above directly with an HTTP client and a MySQL driver.

MySQL, HubSpot and PayPal are already running and are owned by the benchmark. Use them directly. Never stop, kill, replace, reconfigure, or otherwise modify any of these backends, and do not start replacement backends. Do not leave the application running when finished because the benchmark starts and stops it for checks.
